Neuro /uniFB01 nd allows the processing of a single image or several images in bulk. To upload one image, choose Single upload from the top menu and /uniFB01 ll in the necessary information. Upload your image by dragging it or clicking on Select /uniFB01 les and navigating to the folder where the image is stored. Images can only be in NIfTI (.nii, .nii.gz) format. It is important that you have the subject ' s consent to analyse their data in Neuro /uniFB01 nd, so the upload page also asks you to con /uniFB01 rm that you have the necessary approvals before you can select Submit. To upload several images at once, select Multiple upload from the top menu. You will be asked to upload all your images at once along with a CSV /uniFB01 le with all the relevant information about the images. To do this, select Download CSV to view the instructions on how to /uniFB01 ll in the CSV /uniFB01 le and download the template. It is important that you do not include any identi /uniFB01 able information in the CSV /uniFB01 le or elsewhere on the website. Once completed, upload it by pressing Upload CSV. Next, click on Upload scans to upload the images. The processing of the image(s) will start as soon as the upload is completed.

